# Derived by hand from Type System ch. 2 (an element is a plain value until a statement or a host places it) and Semantics ch. 4 (`@Element` of an element is the element statement, at the statement's own path): the button's label follows `$n` in the tick of the click, and its clicks are `!go`'s.
test an_element_value_is_placed

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Button(label="go 0")
    2: Ui.Label(text="went 0")
    3/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="replaced")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Button(label="go 1")

tick 2
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="went 1")
